; The Seatbelt profile of cove-net. Everything is denied, then allowed only what cove-net was seen
; to be refused while it served a card: the rules were found from the denials the kernel logs
; (log show --predicate 'eventMessage CONTAINS "cove-net("'), one at a time.
(version 1)
(deny default)

; The socket of the card is allowed after these rules, by its exact path, as Enter writes it:
; creating it, binding it and accepting its one connection. No other file is.

; The Go runtime reads the number of CPUs again as it runs, to size GOMAXPROCS, and net reads the
; longest backlog of a listener when it listens on the card.
(allow sysctl-read (sysctl-name "hw.ncpu" "kern.ipc.somaxconn"))

; While its exit is the network of the host, cove-net connects to any address, and reads the
; addresses of the interfaces of the host at each connection: the exit refuses the host, not this
; profile, since its addresses change with the network it joins.
(allow network-outbound (remote ip))
(allow sysctl-read (sysctl-name "net.routetable.0.0.3.0"))
